  "experience": {
    "narrative": "You arrive at Le Petit Comptoir, and the atmosphere immediately tells you this place takes food seriously. The Boeuf bourguignon arrives, and you understand why people make pilgrimages here—every element is precisely executed, ingredients at their peak, technique honed over years. Chef sources from same market vendor for 30 years makes this more than just a meal; it's an immersion into the authentic culture of the place. This is the kind of dining that reminds you why you seek out local favorites, why recommendations from residents are gold, why some restaurants transcend mere eating to become essential experiences.",
    "rating": 4.5
  }
